<h1 id="P2"><span lang="EN-GB">Enhance Features</span></h1>
<hr align="left" width="98.974%" size="6" class="whs3">
<p><span lang="EN-GB">This command is accessible from</span> <i style="font-style:normal; font-weight:bold;"><span class="Path" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Mesh &gt; Enhance Features</b></span></i> <span lang="EN-GB">or by pressing</span> <b><span class="Shortcut">Ctrl + J</span></b><span lang="EN-GB">.</span></p>
<p class="Description"><b><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Description:</b></span></b> <span class="Command">Enhance Features</span> <span lang="EN-GB">command detects edges of the visible mesh selection and sharpen them by pulling vertices towards the feature lines. You have three levels of control how strong the sharpness to be.&#160;</span></p>
<p><span lang="EN-GB"><img src="../mesh/Processing_Meshes_files/image007.gif" width="257px" height="164px" border="0" class="img_whs4" alt=""></span></p>
<p><span lang="EN-GB">This command is grayed if there is no selection or all selections are hidden. It works on wholly selected entities as well as on partial selections. Default level for this command is the lowest strength.</span></p>
<p class="Example" style="text-decoration:underline;"><span lang="EN-GB"><a class="dropspot" href="javascript:kadovTextPopup(this)" id="a1" style="text-decoration:underline;">Example</a></span></p>
<div class="droptext" id="POPUP165627064" style="display:'none'; x-ss-type:dropdown;">
<table cellspacing="5" class="whs5">
<col>
<col>
<tr valign="top" class="whs6">
<td class="whs7">
<p><span lang="EN-GB"><img src="../mesh/Processing_Meshes_files/image009.jpg" border="0" class="img_whs8" alt=""></span></p>
</td>
<td class="whs9">
<p><span lang="EN-GB"><img src="../mesh/Processing_Meshes_files/image011.jpg" border="0" class="img_whs8" alt=""></span></p>
